After working on multiple GitOps rollouts with 35+ clusters and 100s of apps, I’ve developed some core tuning principles. Sharing them here so your team doesn’t learn the hard way.

You’ve got 100+ apps. 50+ repos. Multiple clusters.
ArgoCD can handle it — if you configure it for scale.

Here are my top tips for keeping performance high and ops smooth 👇

⚙️ Performance Optimizations:
1. Use Redis Cache
Enable Redis to reduce load on ArgoCD API for heavy diff checks and sync status

2. Tune Application Controller Settings
Increase reconciliation concurrency for large workloads

3. Disable Auto-Sync Diffs When Needed
Reduces Git polling pressure — schedule syncs intentionally

4. Limit Repo Server Cloning
Split large repos or use shallow clones

5. Use ApplicationSets Carefully
Powerful, but generates lots of CRDs — monitor controller performance

🧠 Monitoring Tips:
✅ Enable Prometheus metrics
✅ Use Grafana dashboards for sync status, reconciliation durations
✅ Monitor memory & CPU on Repo Server and App Controller

📌 TL;DR
GitOps at scale needs more than YAML.
Tune, monitor, and architect ArgoCD like the production system it is.
